WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.268
-After the Electoral College

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.336
made it official on Monday,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.171
some Republicans
are now finally admitting

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.939
that Joe Biden will be
the next president

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.841
and many in the GOP
and right-wing media

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.644
are still insisting
there is a way

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.746
for Trump to subvert
the will of the voters

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:14.947
and remain in office.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.316
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:21.254
♪♪

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.689
Been a tough week
for Donald Trump.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.824 line:0%
The Electoral College made
Joe Biden's win official;

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.193 line:0%
Republican leaders began
to finally admit

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.661 line:0%
that Biden will be
the next president,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.996 line:0%
albeit way too late;

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.864
a judge ruled
that Trump's business

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:34.701
must turn over documents sought
as part of an investigation

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.603
by the New York
Attorney General's Office;

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.205
and, on top of all that,
Trump's neighbors in Florida

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.273
went public
with a small request --

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:43.176 line:0%
Please do not move here.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.211
-Trump's neighbors in Florida

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.046
are bracing for the possibility

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:50.416 line:0%
he just might spend
his post-White House days

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.884 line:0%
right there alongside them.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.787 line:0%
Tonight, The Washington Post
is reporting

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:57.290 line:0%
that some of the neighbors
down in Mar-a-Lago

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.691 line:0%
want the city of Palm Beach

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.794 line:0%
to prevent Trump
from settling down there.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.931 line:0%
They argue he signed away
his legal right

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.033 line:0%
to live there full-time
back in the '90s,

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.470 line:0%
when the resort was
originally converted

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.006 line:0%
from a private residence
to a private club.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:16.309
-Just amazing. New Yorkers
don't want him in New York.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.177
His neighbors don't want him
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.547
This is like one of those
ironic punishments

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.615
for a racist
on "The Twilight Zone."

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.384
"We do have a hacienda
available in Mexico City."

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.685
[ As Trump ]
No!

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.788
He's going to be our first
nomad ex-president.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.023
Remember how everyone made fun
of Hillary Clinton

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.759
for taking a walk in the woods,
once, after she lost?

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.194
Trump's going to have
to live in the woods.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.829
Years from now,
a group of hikers

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.832
are going to find him holed up
in a cave, with a long beard,

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.834
doing rallies for a bunch
of polecats.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.069
[ As Trump ]
We love the ferrets,
don't we, folks?

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:45.304
Natural allies.

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:48.507
But the skunks,
how do we feel about the skunks?

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:51.377
Not nice.
Not nice, the skunks.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.112
Trump's ego has obviously
taking a hit this week,

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.213
so his allies have come up

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.681
with an idea
to make him feel better --

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.050
give him credit
for the COVID vaccine

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.185
he had nothing to do with.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.887
Several Fox hosts have suggested

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.554
that it should be called
the Trump vaccine,

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:04.790
and a right-wing columnist
from The Washington Post

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.925
wrote an op-ed called...

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.198
First of all, why should Trump
get credit for the vaccine?

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:15.168
What did he do, besides say
we should make a vaccine?

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.971
I mean, I think we should make
dinner for the kids every night,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.073
but I'm smart enough not
to tell my wife

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.908
we should call it Dad Spaghetti.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.009
Also, you're never going
to unite this country,

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:25.044
and it's crazy to try.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.812
Biden should give
the same speech

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.414
my algebra teacher used to give

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.249
on the first
nice Friday in April.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.350
"I don't want to be here.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.684
You don't want to be here.

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:35.254
Let's just get through this crap
so we can all go home."

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.556
Trump didn't do anything.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:39.092
He's like the guy standing
on the sidewalk,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.626
watching you parallel park.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.395
"You got to cut
the wheels, man."

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.563
Yeah, I know that!

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.630
For a crowd that constantly

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:45.798
claims your feelings
don't matter,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.367
they seem to think
Donald Trump's feelings

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.168
matter a lot,
and especially this week,

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.037
after the Electoral College,
yet again,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.305
confirmed that Trump had lost.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.440
Yesterday at a rally in Georgia,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.609
Biden joked about the fact
that multiple recounts

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.045
in the Electoral College have
confirmed his victory there.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.181
-Thank you for standing strong

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.716
to make sure
your voices were heard,

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.652
your votes were counted,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.786
and counted,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.920
and counted again!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.422
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.691
I'm starting to feel like
I won Georgia three times.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:14.493
-It's true.
Biden's win in Georgia

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.061
has been confirmed three times.

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:18.163
And, in terms of convincing
someone of the truth,

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:21.534
needing three times
is what's known as a Scrooging.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.935
But there you have it,
three times.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.804
Biden's win in Georgia
has been confirmed more times

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.972
than a dentist appointment.
And, Dr. Giotopoulos,

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.507
you don't need
to call me every day

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.042
for three weeks
before the appointment.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.612
Just send me one email,
two days ahead of time,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.280
so I know it's time
to start flossing.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.282
And, yes, I've been
wearing my retainer.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.217
[ Hushed ]
Honey, have you seen
my retainer?

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.586
Also, if Biden's Georgia win
has been confirmed three times,

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:44.023
that means Trump's loss has also
been confirmed three times.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.725
When you get rejected,
it's pretty pathetic

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.761
to double-check once,
let alone three times.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.363
Trump has been
outside Georgia's window,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.131
holding the boom box
three nights in a row

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.666
and, each night,
Georgia shut the window

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.301
and turned on the sprinklers.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.970
And that may seem like a dated
movie reference, but remember,

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.207
Trump's only political
philosophy is "Say Anything."

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.008
Only a true business genius
like Trump

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.077
could parlay
one embarrassing loss

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.280
into multiple
embarrassing losses.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.648
It's like investing in Enron

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:11.050
and then, when it goes bust,
you jump out the window,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.118
but, instead of the sidewalk,
you land on a couch

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:15.721
someone was throwing out
and you fart super loud,

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:18.424
just as a dowager countess
is getting out of a town car.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.125
Trump found a way
to keep reminding people,

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:21.561
on a nearly daily basis,

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.096
that he's now the only
president in history

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.064
to lose the popular vote,
get impeached,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.734
then lose reelection, which is
worse than being forgotten.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.068
Zachary Taylor sucked, too,

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.837
but nobody even remembers
that guy,

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.205
except that he's the only
president in history

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.007
named after two
[bleep] toddlers.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:36.375
Zachary!

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.911
Put that stick --
Because I said so!

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.978
Taylor!

00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:41.013
Where are your pants?

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.314
You don't know?

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:43.716
Zachary!

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.085
Why is your stick bigger?!
[ Growling ] You two!

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.586
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:49.355
On the plus side for Trump,
he's the president

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.323
every kid for the next 100 years

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:53.192
is going to want to do
their oral report on.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.961
Jason, your president is
James K. Polk.

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:57.663
[ As Andy Samberg ]
I don't want that snoozefest!

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.966
I want the guy
who knew Grimace!

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.069
[ Laughing ] Samberg.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.571
[ As Samberg ]
I wanna do the
Grimace president!

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.340
Nobody here gets me!

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.975
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.744
And, yet, the deluded Trump
dead-enders will not give up,

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.178
not because they genuinely think

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.680
there's a path
to staying in power,

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.016
but because they're fully
invested in the belief

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.451
that their opponents
are illegitimate

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.286
and any votes for Democrats
are fraudulent.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.621
On Monday, after the
Electoral College vote,

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:25.425
the far-right network Newsmax
tried to brush it off

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:28.294
like it was some
inconsequential technicality.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.929 line:8%
-There are people, right now,
who are out there,

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:34.233 line:8%
calling Joe Biden
the president-elect.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:39.305 line:8%
Now, at this point,
there is some political

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:42.408 line:8%
and some historical
justification

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.811 line:8%
for them to do so,
at this point.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:47.279 line:7%
I personally feel they're wrong.

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:49.915
-Oh, you personally feel
they're wrong?

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.416
You don't want
your controversial views

00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:53.886
to stain the sterling
journalistic reputation

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.921
of Newsmax, which,
up until recently,

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:58.190
got less attention
than a stand-up comic

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.358
opening at Ozzfest.

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:00.993
"How's everybody doing?!

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.795
You guys ready to thrash?!

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.463
First, first, that's great.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.332
Where are my married guys at?

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.333
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.603
Where are my married guys at?

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.938
Married guys?"

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.405
I don't know much about Newsmax,

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:16.208
but it sounds like the name
of one of those fake news shows

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:19.011
that's really just a late night
infomercial for hair plugs.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.379
"Welcome back to Newsmax.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.114
Our next guest is
the medical genius

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.417
behind the latest breakthrough
in hair science,

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.985
known as paint."

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.686
But, hey, he personally
feels they're wrong

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:29.488
to call Joe Biden
the president-elect,

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:32.391
just like I personally feel
that the 2007 Academy Awards

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.427
were wrong to give Best Actor
to Forest Whitaker

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.895
for "The Last King of Scotland,"

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.830
instead of me, for my role
in" American Dreamz,"

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.032
with Hugh Grant,
who said, to my face,

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.768
about my performance --
and this is real --

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:44.970
"I don't remember it."

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.372
We had scenes together.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.140
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.410 line:0%
The Trump cabal is so committed
to subverting democracy

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.977 line:0%
and painting Biden's win
as illegitimate

00:06:51.977 --> 00:06:54.646 line:0%
that some states even held
fake Electoral College votes

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:56.382 line:0%
and pretended an alternate
slate of electors

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.885 line:0%
would be sent to Congress
to put Trump over the top

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.721
once they, you know,
finally win a court case.

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:04.957 line:8%
As we speak today,
an alternate slate of electors

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:07.493 line:8%
in the contested states
is going to vote

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:10.262 line:8%
and we're going to send
those results up to Congress.

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:14.267 line:8%
This will ensure that all of our
legal remedies remain open.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.901
-Alternate electors?
You might be thinking

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:17.403
of an alternate universe.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.338
"Not only is the president
well on his way

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:22.808
to reelection here on Earth-C,
he is also one step closer

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.910
to apprehending America's
gravest threat,

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.112
Superman,
the villain of Krypton."

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:30.450
And I'm sorry, but none of your
legal remedies remain open.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.318
You guys lost
almost 60 court cases,

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:34.520
including two
at the Supreme Court.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.755
At this point, you're the kid
at the spelling bee

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:39.291
who's buying time
by continuing to list letters.

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:40.426
"We're going to stop
you there, Kyle.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:42.227
Pheromone doesn't start
with an "F,"

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:45.731
and I think we both know
it doesn't have 35 E's."

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:48.267
And, no, you didn't just lose
on a technicality,

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.769 line:0%
as Trump and his allies
have continued to claim.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:51.903 line:7%
-They're winning these things

00:07:51.903 --> 00:07:53.339 line:7%
on little technicalities,

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.707 line:7%
like a thing called standing.

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.275
-Standing is not a technicality.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.709
It means you don't even
have the right

00:07:57.709 --> 00:07:59.244
to bring the case.
That's like saying --

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:00.646
[ As Trump ]
They won't let me play
Little League

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.248
because of the technicality

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:03.916
that I'm not nine years old.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.518
Though I do you think
it's worth pausing,

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:06.752
while we're putting
so much emphasis

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.954
on the Electoral College,
to remind everyone

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:11.223
that the Electoral College
is a terrible system

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:13.425
and the way you can tell
it's a bad system

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:16.295
is the majority of Americans
want to get rid of it.

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.662
And it felt that way
for decades,

00:08:17.662 --> 00:08:18.664
but it's still there.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.198
If you're a sane, normal person,

00:08:20.198 --> 00:08:22.534
you might have assumed that the
presidential election was over

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:23.836
the moment it became clear

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:26.405
that Joe Biden would get
more votes than Donald Trump.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.206
That's how it works
in most democracies,

00:08:28.206 --> 00:08:30.109
with the exception of Norway,
of course,

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.911
where the prime minister
is chosen

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:34.613
by a mystical gnome named Lars,
who emerges from his cave

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:37.049
once every four years
and names a new leader,

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.284
in exchange for fish balls
and orange soda.

00:08:39.284 --> 00:08:42.555 line:0%
And that's today's...
[ Shimmering tune plays ]

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:45.725 line:0%
Of course, in Norway,
they chant...

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:47.025 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:48.994 line:0%
And that's today's...

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:51.630 line:0%
[ Crickets chirping ]

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.431 line:0%
[ Laughing ] Which still
did better with the crew

00:08:53.431 --> 00:08:54.700
than every other joke.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.235
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.336
We'll put in the crickets.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.171
You won't hear it
over the crew laughing.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.807
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.343
Although it might actually
be preferable

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:06.745
to have a system like that
because, instead,

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:09.348
we have the Electoral College,
which, every four years,

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.550
anoints a handful
of swing states as kingmakers

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.952
and has awarded the presidency

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.420
to the loser of the popular
vote several times.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.922
I mean, remember, Joe Biden got

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:19.525
seven million more votes
than Donald Trump,

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.493
out of a total of 158 million.

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:24.230
But if you flip
about 65,000 combined votes

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.564 line:0%
in the right states,
Trump would win

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.600 line:0%
the Electoral College,
and that's insane.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.034
We don't do anything else
like that.

00:09:29.034 --> 00:09:30.435
When the Steelers
score a touchdown,

00:09:30.435 --> 00:09:32.104
it's not worth 47 points,

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:33.639
just because they're
from a swing state,

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:36.575
although that would be
very helpful, right now.

00:09:36.575 --> 00:09:38.911
Anyway, the Electoral College
is a ticking time bomb

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.245
that is inevitably going to lead

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:42.847
to a major crisis of democratic
legitimacy one day.

00:09:42.847 --> 00:09:44.517
Arguably, it already has.

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.452
It's just that Democrats,
unlike Republicans,

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:47.886
accept the results of elections.

00:09:47.886 --> 00:09:49.922
And it's not even like
the Electoral College

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.723
was carefully crafted
by the founders

00:09:51.723 --> 00:09:54.293
and designed as an integral
component of our democracy.

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:55.995
In fact,
they basically left it

00:09:55.995 --> 00:09:58.464
until the last minute of the
Constitutional Convention,

00:09:58.464 --> 00:10:00.366
then half-assed it
so they could all go home.

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:03.535
-1787, the founders, you know,

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:04.770
they go to Philadelphia,

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.004
the framers of the Constitution,

00:10:06.004 --> 00:10:07.339
create this new document,

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:08.841
which has a president,
for the first time,

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:10.543
and they have to decide
"How are we going

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:12.344
to choose the president," right?

00:10:12.344 --> 00:10:15.914
And it is the most vexing
question for the whole summer.

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:18.216
They fight about it
for weeks on end.

00:10:18.216 --> 00:10:19.418
And then they come up
with this system

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:21.386
in the waning days
of the convention,

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:23.555
primarily because they were
completely exhausted.

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:25.324
They wanted to get
the hell out of there.

00:10:25.324 --> 00:10:27.192
And, you know, James Madison
admits it after the fact.

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:29.729
He basically says,
"Yeah, you know what?

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.397
We were pretty tired
at that point."

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:33.399
-The founders approached
the Electoral College

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:35.000
with all the energy of fans

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.668
at the seventh inning
of a Mets game.

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:38.904
"If we leave now,
we can beat the horse traffic.

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:40.606
Wait, hold on.
Hold on.

00:10:40.606 --> 00:10:42.241
I can't find my teeth."

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:44.143
And it's also worth noting
that, almost immediately,

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:46.378
the founders realized
our system was broken

00:10:46.378 --> 00:10:48.380
and wasn't operating
the way they intended.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.549
They didn't think we'd devolve
into a situation

00:10:50.549 --> 00:10:52.384
where we have to pray
that Florida

00:10:52.384 --> 00:10:53.852
finally pulls it together,

00:10:53.852 --> 00:10:55.454
like we're Zachary
and Taylor's mom

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:57.222
at the kindergarten
Christmas pageant.

00:10:57.222 --> 00:10:58.724
"Just please behave
for one night.

00:10:58.724 --> 00:10:59.992
Zachary!

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:03.228
Why would Joseph have
a light saber?!

00:11:03.228 --> 00:11:06.431
What -- I'm sorry --
what part of the Bible, Taylor,

00:11:06.431 --> 00:11:08.400
is a wise man
not wearing pants?!

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.501
Zachary!

00:11:09.501 --> 00:11:11.036
Taylor!

00:11:11.036 --> 00:11:12.671
[ Growling ]
Oh, these two!"

00:11:12.671 --> 00:11:14.406
[ Laughter ]

00:11:14.406 --> 00:11:15.841
The founders just wanted
to go home,

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:17.042
so they scratched out
a half-baked

00:11:17.042 --> 00:11:19.211
Electoral College system
at the last minute,

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:20.479
then got the hell out of there.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.581
There's a reason there's
no rap battle in "Hamilton"

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:24.316
about the creation
of the Electoral College,

00:11:24.316 --> 00:11:28.020
even though I thought
my audition was very convincing.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.422
♪ Sit back, everybody,
as I drop, a little knowledge ♪

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:32.924
♪ About the E to the L
to the ectoral College ♪

00:11:32.924 --> 00:11:34.660
Shoemaker,
when you raise the roof,

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.562
you go like this,
and you're going like this.

00:11:36.562 --> 00:11:39.365
[ Laughter ]
Oh, you want me to stop? Why?

00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:40.365
It's bad?

00:11:40.365 --> 00:11:43.335
Yeah, but all raps start bad.

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:44.703
Well, agree to disagree.

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:46.171
You know what?
Let's have this fight later.

00:11:46.171 --> 00:11:48.974
The Electoral College should be
abolished for the obvious reason

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:50.843
that, in a democracy,
everyone's vote should matter

00:11:50.843 --> 00:11:52.344
and whoever gets the most votes
should win.

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:54.145
But abolishing
the Electoral College

00:11:54.145 --> 00:11:55.480
would also have
the added benefit

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.816
of preventing future attempts
to steal the election,

00:11:57.816 --> 00:12:00.519
through Congress or state
legislatures, or the courts,

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:01.553
just like the one we just saw.

00:12:01.553 --> 00:12:02.888
The presidency would go

00:12:02.888 --> 00:12:04.523
to whoever got the most votes

00:12:04.523 --> 00:12:06.391
and that's it.
It would be simple.

00:12:06.391 --> 00:12:08.293
It would be like
how a democracy works

00:12:08.293 --> 00:12:10.161
or how any election,
anywhere, works.

00:12:10.161 --> 00:12:12.464
In high school,
all the kids vote

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:14.633
for who they think
gave the funniest speech,

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:16.969
and then that person
is class president.

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:19.204
Not like the students vote
and then the prom king,

00:12:19.204 --> 00:12:20.773
a math teacher,
and the kid with the pet iguana

00:12:20.773 --> 00:12:22.775
get in a room
and decide if they're right.

00:12:22.775 --> 00:12:24.876
And, if it was a simple case
and most votes win,

00:12:24.876 --> 00:12:27.113
you wouldn't have Rudy and his
gang of cartoon characters

00:12:27.113 --> 00:12:30.148
descending on state capitals
after one too many Jaegerbombs

00:12:30.148 --> 00:12:31.584
at the local Houlihan's.

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:34.320
Democrats need to pursue major
reforms to our institutions,

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.922
to ensure that something like
this can't happen in the future,

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:39.257
otherwise, it will happen
in the future.

00:12:39.257 --> 00:12:41.293
Republicans made it very clear
that, if given the chance,

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:43.261
they will do everything possible
to steal an election

00:12:43.261 --> 00:12:45.564
through the courts, Congress,
or state legislatures,

00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:47.633
and the existence
of the Electoral College

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.701
makes such an outcome
much more likely,

00:12:49.701 --> 00:12:50.969
even if Republicans
don't have...

00:12:50.969 --> 00:12:52.404 line:7%
-A thing called standing.

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:54.173
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:54.173 --> 00:12:57.442
♪♪

